                                "prompt": "Write a Java program/method for the following problem:\n\n**Write a Java method countWords(String str) that returns the number of words in a given string.**",
                                "model_answer": "```java\npublic int countWords ( String str ) {\n// Check if the string is null or completely empty . If so ,\nit contains 0 words .\nif ( str == null || str . trim (). isEmpty ()) {\nreturn 0;\n}\n// trim () removes leading and trailing spaces .\n// split (\"\\\\ s+\") divides the string into an array of words\nbased on one or more spaces .\nString [] words = str . trim (). split ( \"\\\\ s+\");\n// The length of the resulting array is the total word\ncount .\nreturn words . length ;\n}\n```",
                                "solutionCode": "public int countWords ( String str ) {\n// Check if the string is null or completely empty . If so ,\nit contains 0 words .\nif ( str == null || str . trim (). isEmpty ()) {\nreturn 0;\n}\n// trim () removes leading and trailing spaces .\n// split (\"\\\\ s+\") divides the string into an array of words\n// based on one or more spaces .\nString [] words = str . trim (). split ( \"\\\\ s+\");\n// The length of the resulting array is the total word\n// count .\nreturn words . length ;\n}",
