                                "question": "Q2. Design a class Computer with attributes brand and ram. Create a subclass Laptop that adds a weight attribute and overrides the toString() method. Write a test program to instantiate both.",
                                "prompt": "Write a Java program/method for the following problem:\n\n**Design a class Computer with attributes brand and ram. Create a subclass Laptop that adds a weight attribute and overrides the toString() method. Write a test program to instantiate both.**",
                                "model_answer": "```java\nclass Computer {\nString brand ;\nint ram ;\n// Constructor to initialize the parent fields\npublic Computer ( String brand , int ram ) {\nthis . brand = brand ;\nthis . ram = ram ;\n}\npublic String toString () {\nreturn \" Computer : \" + brand + \", RAM : \" + ram + \"GB \";\n}\n}\nclass Laptop extends Computer {\ndouble weight ;\n// Constructor of subclass must call the parent\nconstructor using super ()\npublic Laptop ( String brand , int ram , double weight ) {\nsuper ( brand , ram ); // Initialize inherited fields\nthis . weight = weight ; // Initialize specific field\n}\n@Override\npublic String toString () {\n// super . toString () calls the parent 's method , then we\nappend the new info\nreturn super . toString () + \", Weight : \" + weight + \"kg \"\n;\n}\n}\npublic class TestPC {\npublic static void main ( String [] args ) {\nComputer desktop = new Computer ( \" Dell \", 8);\nLaptop macbook = new Laptop ( \" Apple \", 16 , 1.2) ;\n// Demonstrating dynamic binding / polymorphism\nimplicitly via print\nSystem . out . println ( desktop . toString ());\nSystem . out . println ( macbook . toString ());\n}\n}\n```",
                                "solutionCode": "class Computer {\nString brand ;\nint ram ;\n// Constructor to initialize the parent fields\npublic Computer ( String brand , int ram ) {\nthis . brand = brand ;\nthis . ram = ram ;\n}\npublic String toString () {\nreturn \" Computer : \" + brand + \", RAM : \" + ram + \"GB \";\n}\n}\nclass Laptop extends Computer {\ndouble weight ;\n// Constructor of subclass must call the parent\n// constructor using super ()\npublic Laptop ( String brand , int ram , double weight ) {\nsuper ( brand , ram ); // Initialize inherited fields\nthis . weight = weight ; // Initialize specific field\n}\n@Override\npublic String toString () {\n// super . toString () calls the parent 's method , then we\nappend the new info\nreturn super . toString () + \", Weight : \" + weight + \"kg \"\n;\n}\n}\nclass TestPC {\npublic static void main ( String [] args ) {\nComputer desktop = new Computer ( \" Dell \", 8);\nLaptop macbook = new Laptop ( \" Apple \", 16 , 1.2) ;\n// Demonstrating dynamic binding / polymorphism\n// implicitly via print\nSystem . out . println ( desktop . toString ());\nSystem . out . println ( macbook . toString ());\n}\n}",
