                                "question": "Q3. Write a Java method isPrime(int num) that returns true if the number is prime, and false otherwise.",
                                "prompt": "Write a Java program/method for the following problem:\n\n**Write a Java method isPrime(int num) that returns true if the number is prime, and false otherwise.**",
                                "model_answer": "```java\npublic boolean isPrime ( int num ) {\n// Numbers less than or equal to 1 are not prime by\ndefinition .\nif ( num <= 1) return false ;\n// We only need to check up to num / 2 (or Math . sqrt ( num )\nfor better performance ).\nfor (int i = 2; i <= num / 2; i ++) {\n// If the number is evenly divisible by any 'i ', it is\nnot prime .\nif ( num % i == 0) return false ;\n}\n// If the loop finishes without returning false , the\nnumber is prime .\nreturn true ;\n}\n```",
