                                "prompt": "Write a Java program/method for the following problem:\n\n**Design a class Stock containing symbol, name, previousClosingPrice, and currentPrice. Write a method getChangePercent() that calculates the percentage change, and a test program.**",
                                "model_answer": "```java\nclass Stock {\nString symbol ;\nString name ;\ndouble previousClosingPrice ;\ndouble currentPrice ;\n// Constructor initializes the symbol and name\npublic Stock ( String symbol , String name ) {\nthis . symbol = symbol ;\nthis . name = name ;\n}\n// Method to calculate the percentage difference\npublic double getChangePercent () {\n// Formula : (( New - Old ) / Old ) * 100\nreturn (( currentPrice - previousClosingPrice ) /\npreviousClosingPrice ) * 100;\n}\n}\nclass TestStock {\npublic static void main ( String [] args ) {\nStock s = new Stock (\" SUNW \", \"Sun Microsystems \");\ns. previousClosingPrice = 100;\ns. currentPrice = 90; // Price dropped\nSystem . out . println (\" Price Change : \" + s.\ngetChangePercent () + \"%\");\n}\n}\n```",
