                                "question": "Question 1: Custom Power Method",
                                "prompt": "### Question 1: Custom Power Method\n\nWrite a method `power(double x, int y)` that calculates $x^y$ without using `Math.pow()`.",
                                "solutionCode": "public class PowerCalculator {\n    public static double power(double x, int y) {\n        double result = 1.0;\n        int exponent = Math.abs(y);\n        for (int i = 0; i < exponent; i++) {\n            result *= x;\n        }\n        if (y < 0) {\n            return 1.0 / result;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(\"2^3 = \" + power(2, 3));\n        System.out.println(\"5^-2 = \" + power(5, -2));\n    }\n}",
                                "model_answer": "```java\npublic class PowerCalculator {\n    public static double power(double x, int y) {\n        double result = 1.0;\n        int exponent = Math.abs(y);\n        for (int i = 0; i < exponent; i++) {\n            result *= x;\n        }\n        if (y < 0) {\n            return 1.0 / result;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n```",
                                "hint": "Loop |y| times multiplying result by x. Handle negative exponents by returning 1.0 / result."
